# KiCad PCB Layout - Interdigitated Soil Moisture Sensor
# Enhanced design with soldermask, air reference, and guard ring

# PCB Specifications
# - Size: 50mm x 35mm (increased for better electrode design)
# - Layers: 2 (Top and Bottom)
# - Thickness: 1.6mm
# - Copper weight: 1oz
# - Soldermask: Green (over copper traces)

# Electrode Design Specifications
# - Primary Sensor: 25mm x 15mm interdigitated electrodes
# - Air Reference: 10mm x 10mm interdigitated electrodes  
# - Guard Ring: 2mm wide trace surrounding sensor areas
# - Finger width: 0.5mm
# - Finger spacing: 0.5mm
# - Finger length: 10mm (primary), 5mm (reference)

# Primary Soil Sensor Electrodes (Top Layer)
# Location: Center of PCB (25mm x 15mm area)
# Design: Interdigitated fingers with soldermask overlay
#
# Electrode A (connected to oscillator input):
# - 12 fingers, each 0.5mm wide x 10mm long
# - Spacing: 0.5mm between fingers
# - Total width: 11.5mm (12 * 0.5mm + 11 * 0.5mm spacing)
# - Connected to 74HC14 Pin 1 (oscillator input)
#
# Electrode B (connected to oscillator output):
# - 12 fingers, each 0.5mm wide x 10mm long  
# - Spacing: 0.5mm between fingers
# - Interleaved with Electrode A
# - Connected to 74HC14 Pin 2 (oscillator output)
#
# Soldermask: Applied over entire electrode area
# - Prevents direct contact with soil
# - Reduces corrosion and contamination
# - Maintains capacitive coupling through soldermask

# Air Reference Electrodes (Top Layer)
# Location: Top-right corner (10mm x 10mm area)
# Design: Interdigitated fingers WITHOUT soldermask
#
# Reference Electrode A (connected to oscillator input):
# - 8 fingers, each 0.5mm wide x 5mm long
# - Spacing: 0.5mm between fingers
# - Connected to 74HC14 Pin 1 (oscillator input)
#
# Reference Electrode B (connected to oscillator output):
# - 8 fingers, each 0.5mm wide x 5mm long
# - Spacing: 0.5mm between fingers
# - Interleaved with Reference Electrode A
# - Connected to 74HC14 Pin 2 (oscillator output)
#
# No Soldermask: Exposed copper for air reference
# - Provides temperature compensation baseline
# - Measures environmental changes
# - Compensates for oscillator drift

# Guard Ring (Top Layer)
# Location: Surrounding both sensor areas
# Design: 2mm wide copper trace
#
# Guard Ring Features:
# - Connected to 74HC14 Pin 2 (oscillator output)
# - Surrounds primary sensor area (25mm x 15mm)
# - Surrounds air reference area (10mm x 10mm)
# - 2mm clearance from electrode edges
# - Bootstrap effect reduces parasitic capacitance
# - Minimizes fringe field effects
# - Improves measurement stability

# Component Placement (Top Layer)
# 
# Power Supply Section (Top Left):
# - AMS1117-3.3V regulator
# - Input capacitor: 100uF
# - Output capacitor: 100uF
# - Input: 5V (J1)
# - Output: 3.3V rail
#
# 74HC14 Section (Left Center):
# - U1: 74HC14 (DIP-14)
# - R1: 10kΩ resistor (timing)
# - C1: 100nF decoupling capacitor
# - C2: Variable capacitor (soil sensor)
# - C3: Variable capacitor (air reference)
#
# ATTINY85 Section (Bottom Left):
# - U2: ATTINY85 (DIP-8)
# - C4: 100nF decoupling capacitor
# - R2: 10kΩ pull-up resistor (reset)
# - J2: Programming header (6-pin)
#
# CubeCell Section (Bottom Right):
# - U3: CubeCell module (SMD)
# - C5: 100nF decoupling capacitor
# - Antenna connector (optional)

# Trace Routing:
# - Power traces: 0.5mm width
# - Signal traces: 0.25mm width
# - Guard ring: 2mm width
# - Electrode traces: 0.5mm width
# - Ground plane: Bottom layer (avoid under sensor areas)
# - VCC plane: Top layer (where possible)

# Via Specifications:
# - Size: 0.2mm drill, 0.4mm pad
# - Plated through holes
# - Minimum 4 vias for power distribution
# - No vias in sensor areas

# Silkscreen Labels:
# - Component designators
# - Pin numbers
# - Power indicators
# - Sensor area markings
# - "SOLDERSIDE" marking on sensor area
# - "AIR REFERENCE" marking on reference area

# Solder Mask:
# - Green solder mask
# - Applied over primary sensor electrodes
# - NOT applied over air reference electrodes
# - Exposed pads for programming header
# - Exposed pads for power connector

# Assembly Notes:
# - All components on top layer
# - CubeCell module requires reflow soldering
# - Other components can be hand-soldered
# - Primary sensor area must be protected from moisture
# - Air reference area must remain exposed to air
# - Guard ring must be connected to oscillator output

# Testing Considerations:
# - Measure capacitance between electrode pairs
# - Verify guard ring connection to oscillator output
# - Test temperature compensation with air reference
# - Calibrate with known moisture levels
# - Verify soldermask integrity over primary sensor
